# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the JS bundle at build time by Expo -
# they are not secret once the app ships (any user can extract them from the
# binary), which is fine here: RevenueCat's public SDK keys are designed to be
# shipped inside client apps (unlike your App Store Connect API key, which
# stays server-side only and is never entered here).

# From RevenueCat dashboard -> Project -> API Keys -> Public app-specific key (iOS)
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_API_KEY=

# From RevenueCat dashboard -> Project -> API Keys -> Public app-specific key (Android)
EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_PURCHASES - web design preview ONLY. Leave unset.
#
# Set to 1 to swap the store for a local mock that grants lifetime access
# without charging anything:
#
#     EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_PURCHASES=1 npx expo start --web
#
# It must be an explicit opt-in and never a fallback. The mock used to be
# selected simply because no RevenueCat key was present on web, which meant
# `expo export --platform web` on a machine without .env.local produced a
# bundle that handed out paid access to every visitor. Without this flag the
# app fails CLOSED: purchases are unavailable and the paywall says so.
#
# Never set it in an EAS build profile (see eas.json) or in production.
